WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:06.580
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and this week on
Teen Wolf was like the intervention episodes

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.190
of How I Met Your Mother, except it was How
I Met Your Beta starring Liam.

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.990
We got a nice resolution in the Scott Liam
story or at least a big wolf step forward.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.849
But I think the real surprise was Funny Derek.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.900
Who knew Tyler Hoechlin was allowed to be
so funny?

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.119
Hello any new people, if you're just finding
me for the first time I do weekly Teen Wolf

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:23.119
videos.

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:24.119
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:27.460
I'm even doing a special comic con giveaway
that I'll explain after my episode review.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:32.430
I'm going to start with my top 5 wtf moments
and then my review.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.490
Careful for spoilers if you haven't seen the
episode yet.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:38.340
I'll wait just a sec...Okay, here we go.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:41.480
Number 5 - Batman Derek and Sheriff Stalinski

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:45.200
Derek has been so much more fun this season
since getting his mojo stolen by Kate.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.640
It's like he's got this whole new personality
that allows him to be funny.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.680
Batman Derek was funny in a meta way, just
because it made you think of Sheriff Stalinski

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.600
like Gordon.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.320
Their moments together ended up being every
bit as funny as the more traditional funny

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.760
scenes like with Malia and Stiles or Kira
falling down stairs in slow motion.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:10.790
I didn't know Tyler Hoechlin was allowed to
be so funny as Derek, like when he and Chris

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.990
Argent were chained up in the police station.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:20.390
Or when he was laying the sass on Peter about
Mute's not being able to talk.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:23.430
Normally someone like Hoechlin would be the
lead of a show, like it would be written from

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.090
his perspective, not Tyler Poseys.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:28.890
It is an ensemble cast, but Derek is a supporting
character.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:32.380
So in exchange for all the awful things the
writers do to him every year.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.799
They give him all the most gratuitous scenes.

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:38.220
Like he gets to be the Batman of the series.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.320
He totally deserves it too, they've torn him
to pieces, taken away his alpha powers, killed

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.000
almost everyone he's ever loved and now they've
taken his true essence.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.100
Add to that this season, Peter looks like
he's going to take advantage of his weakened

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.050
emotional state.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:58.400
Number 4 - Peter's Old Habits Die Hard

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.130
Him killing the Mute was pure revenge for
the Axe to the chest.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:03.380
Sheriff Stalinksi and Derek were going to
question him before Peter clawed his face

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.240
off.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:09.239
I'm surprised Peter didn't take the opportunity
to throw Derek's joke about Mute's talking

00:02:09.239 --> 00:02:14.550
back in his face, but it wasn't really a moment
for that kind of humor and his actual cool

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:17.400
guy walk away line was way better.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.750
Last season Peter's secret goal was all about
learning the truth about Malia, now that he's

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.370
found her what could his secret plan be?

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.109
And how would he use Derek?

00:02:25.109 --> 00:02:29.650
I think it has something to do with his true
essence that Kate stole.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:32.400
I'm wondering if Peter's going to try and
use that to restore his Alpha powers.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.409
If that's even possible.

00:02:33.409 --> 00:02:37.689
Deucalion told them about absorbing your beta's
life force by killing him.

00:02:37.689 --> 00:02:40.159
So maybe Peter is going to do something like
that.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:43.360
He already killed Derek's sister Lucy to become
the Alpha once.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.510
There's nothing stopping him from trying again
with Derek.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.569
At least once Derek gets back what Kate took
from him.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:54.050
Peter getting his Alpha powers back is also
a nice mirror for getting his money back.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:57.090
Number 3 - Malia versus the Full Moon

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.590
She and Stiles are probably my favorite pair
on the show right now, they're a lot more

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:03.310
fun than Scott and Kira and they seem a lot
closer too.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:08.180
I guess because what they've been through
in some way is more traumatic.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:11.999
Maybe because they've both killed people and
been on the outside of the group for a big

00:03:11.999 --> 00:03:12.999
chunk of last year.

00:03:12.999 --> 00:03:14.319
Any scene they're in turns into some adorable
Malia doesn't understand moment and even when

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:17.370
it got super intense in the basement I never
thought the show would go super dark and make

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:18.370
her maul Stiles.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:21.699
Her story as it relates to Peter is still
a huge question mark, I'm still waiting for

00:03:21.699 --> 00:03:22.829
them to follow up on that.

00:03:22.829 --> 00:03:26.139
Stiles is her anchor so I don't think she'd
ever leave him.

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:29.519
But I do wonder if Stiles would ever leave
the Pack to go with her.

00:03:29.519 --> 00:03:32.469
If she ever did want to go away to get to
know Peter better.

00:03:32.469 --> 00:03:42.260
If any of you watch Arrow, remember at the
end of season 2 how Thea chose to go with

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:43.260
Merlyn.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.089
Number 2 - Lydia Decodes The Deadpool List

00:03:46.089 --> 00:03:51.840
So just a quick heads up, during this scene
there was an issue with the broadcast where

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:56.180
the audio dropped out and you couldn't hear
Lydia and Mason talking.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.010
It was in that record player room with the
freaky wall.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:02.370
That wasn't a special effect or anything,
the audio messed up and MTV posted the clip

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:10.389
with the correct audio on the official teen
wolf website.

00:04:10.389 --> 00:04:13.160
The Deadpool list is the whole impetus for
the killings this year.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.819
Here's a shot of it.

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:17.269
Look at what certain people are worth.

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:21.120
It's implied that the more powerful people
are, the more you get paid for killing them.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:30.320
Who is this person Carrie Hudson who's worth
twice as much as Scott, a true alpha?

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:35.470
Does it not completely suck that Kira is only
worth 6 dollars, Derek is only worth 15 and

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:36.480
Lydia 20.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:40.430
Malia's not on the list we saw, but I think
that they just showed us part of the list,

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:42.190
I think the full one is longer.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:46.260
It's like Scott's Pack collectively is barely
worth one of the normal supers on the list

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:47.260
put together.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:48.260
Some of the names are unfamiliar.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.340
So presumably we'll meet them in the next
several episodes.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:56.130
The Benefactor, as we learned from Werewolf
Beer Delivery Man, is paying out mercenaries

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.130
to kill supers.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:05:02.730
Side note too, we also learned during that
reveal that Liam's friends were mercenaries.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:05.450
He's not on the list just like Malia, but
that doesn't mean he won't end up on it before

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.450
the end of the season.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.940
and my Number 1 WTF Moment - Scott Gives Liam
an Intervention

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:14.920
More than anything the WTF moments in this
episode were funny moments, and the rapid

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:21.750
way this deteriorated from the bite, to the
bath tub to the lake house was just hilarious.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:25.720
It reminded me of the How I Met Your Mother
Intervention episodes.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.690
Liam, you have a problem.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:31.710
In case you missed it, Scott was basically
quoting Derek the whole episode.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:33.030
"Liam, We're Brothers now."

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:34.960
The Bite is a gift.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:38.230
Even Chris Argent had to tell Scott to just
do his own thing.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:42.450
Like he had completely spaced on the fact
Derek is a terrible people person.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:46.050
So he was just replicating his own terrible
experience becoming a werewolf.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:49.290
Liam is still a big question mark right now
in terms of character development.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:54.080
Scott and Derek came to blows before turning
into BFFs in season 3, so I wouldn't be surprised

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:57.380
if Liam went a little nuts on him before the
end of the season.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:05.030
There still the unanswered question of why
Liam smashed up that Teacher's car at his

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:06.640
last school, he said that's what he did to
get kicked out.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.460
But he didn't explain why he did it.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:12.980
When he smashed it up he wrote "It's your
fault" on the car, and we have no idea what

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.070
that means.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:18.560
Liam has currently dethroned Derek as the
angriest character on the show.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:22.300
Somebody give him a giant wolf size chill
pill.

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:26.111
But now it's your turn, let me know what your
favorite moment was and do you think Liam

00:06:26.111 --> 00:06:31.710
is going to chill and be a good beta to Scott,
or is it going to blow up in their faces?

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.880
Don't forget, this is only the first half
of the season.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:36.750
At Comic Con next week, they're going to air
the trailer for 4b, the second batch of episodes

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:37.750
that will air next year.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.700
That will be a whole different plot.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:43.210
But overall this episode was again, my new
favorite.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:48.310
I gave it an A just because I'm super impressed
anytime a show can continue to build the energy

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:51.470
of a story consistently for this many episodes.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:56.610
Usually what you'd see would be some one off
episode to stop the action dead in it's tracks,

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:59.700
but I like that Teen Wolf has chosen to go
more serialized.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:01.630
It's something that Game of Thrones does too.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:06.440
The story each week builds on what happened
last week, it's not like a bunch of one-off

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.330
stories that don't connect or anything.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:12.660
I love what they're doing with Derek by making
him like the supernatural Batman of the season,

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.270
helping Sheriff Stalinski solve the deadpool
murders.

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:18.590
We're still learning about the Benefactor,
and because of the way they're teasing Liam's

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:23.410
friends as mercenaries and Batman Derek hitting
the problem from different angles, I think

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:33.880
all of the characters will learn who it is
at the same time.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:37.760
I'm also wondering how Parrish fits into all
this, I love how they're kind of pairing him

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:39.020
with Lydia so far.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.410
She did make that comment that she's over
dating High School boys, so either that means

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:45.790
she's going to hook up with Parrish or she's
just going to spend a lot of time with him

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:46.790
solving murders.

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:49.960
That just reminds me of the X-Files, but Parrish
isn't really a match for Mulder yet.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:52.040
Lydia I could buy as Sculley.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:56.590
So big hanging questions after the episode
are, who is the Benefactor and who is that

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:59.060
person that's worth twice as much as everyone
else.

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:00.280
Carrie Hudson.

